      "marks": 4,
      "answer": "$\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2ye^x-y^2}{2y-e^x}$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "State the correct derivative of $ye^{2x}$: $2ye^{2x}+e^{2x}\\frac{dy}{dx}$ - B1. State the correct derivative of $y^2e^x$: $y^2e^x+2ye^x\\frac{dy}{dx}$ - B1. Equate an attempted derivative of the left side to zero and solve for $dy/dx$ - M1. Obtain $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2ye^x-y^2}{2y-e^x}$ - A1; condone multiplication by $-1/-1$ and cancellation of $e^x$ without comment. Alternative: rearrange as $y=\\frac2{e^{2x}-ye^x}$, hence $\\frac d{dx}(e^{2x}-ye^x)=2e^{2x}-ye^x-e^x\\frac{dy}{dx}$ - B1. Then $\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac2{(e^{2x}-ye^x)^2}(2e^{2x}-ye^x-e^x\\frac{dy}{dx})$ - B1. Other rearrangements are possible, for example $y=2e^{-2x}+y^2e^{-x}$, giving $\\frac d{dx}(y^2e^{-x})=2ye^{-x}\\frac{dy}{dx}-y^2e^{-x}$ and hence $\\frac{dy}{dx}=-4e^{-2x}+2ye^{-x}\\frac{dy}{dx}-y^2e^{-x}$. Solve for $dy/dx$ - M1. Obtain the given answer - A1. Printed total: 4.",
